# Code Documentation

This codebase is mostly AI-written. Comments are the guide a developer reads first, so document everything. This extends "Public documentation" in `code-quality.mdc`: private helpers get docs too.

## File headers

Every source file (TS, TSX, Swift, config plugins) starts with a short header: what the file is for, where it sits in the architecture (View / ViewModel / Model / native bridge / widget), and what it talks to.

```ts
/**
 * Live Activity command queue (Model layer).
 * Runs start/update/end commands in order against a LiveActivityPresenter so rapid
 * taps can never leave a zombie activity. Used by create-live-activity-controller.ts.
 */
```

## Functions, hooks, components, types

- Every function, hook, component, and Swift method gets a doc comment (JSDoc `/** */` in TS, `///` in Swift): purpose, params, return value, side effects, thrown errors.
- Every exported type, interface, and enum gets a doc comment, and so does each non-obvious field (units, ranges, null meaning).

```ts
/** Snapshot of a running or paused session. All times are epoch milliseconds. */
type TimerSession = {
  /** When the current running stretch began; null while paused. */
  runningSinceMs: number | null;
  /** Time already banked from earlier running stretches. */
  accumulatedMs: number;
};
```

## Inline comments

- Explain **why** and any constraint the code can't show: platform limits, ordering requirements, race conditions, iOS/ActivityKit quirks, workarounds.
- Mark multi-step logic with a short comment per step.
- Don't restate the code (`// increment i`) or narrate history (`// changed from X`, `// added by AI`).

```swift
// ActivityKit matches activities by type name, so this struct must stay
// byte-identical to the copy in modules/study-timer-activity/ios.
```

## Tests

- Each `describe` block gets a one-line comment naming the requirement or edge case it covers.
- Comment any non-obvious setup (fake timers, fake presenters, injected clocks).

## Keep comments true

- When behavior changes, update its comments in the same edit. A stale comment is a bug.
